Third-party components
----------------------
Kerotakis links or embeds the following. All are permissively licensed or
public-domain and compatible with AGPL-3.0 distribution; their notices are
preserved per their respective terms.

Currently shipped
- IPhreeqc / PHREEQC — USGS User Rights Notice (public-domain-like, U.S.
  Geological Survey). Aqueous speciation, mineral saturation, gas partitioning
  and redox. Built from the vendored source and embedded together with its
  thermodynamic databases (phreeqc.dat, wateq4f.dat, minteq.v4.dat,
  pitzer.dat), distributed under the same terms. Those databases carry their
  own literature citations in their comments; Kerotakis surfaces them rather
  than stripping them, so an answer can name the work its numbers rest on.
- Rust crates — serde, thiserror, postcard and their dependencies, all MIT
  and/or Apache-2.0. The full dependency set and its licences are reproduced
  in-app under About -> Open-source licenses, generated from cargo-about.

Planned, not yet shipped (recorded here so the intent is public)
- MY-BASIC — MIT, Copyright (c) 2011–2026 Tony Wang. Pinned, in-progress
  replacement language core for PHREEQC BASIC programs; currently available
  only through the development-only `my-basic-preview` build feature.
- Indigo — Apache-2.0, Copyright (c) EPAM Systems. Structure handling, reaction
  product enumeration, and canonical identity via its bundled IUPAC InChI
  plugin (InChI v1.07+, MIT, Copyright (c) the InChI Project).
- feos, vle-thermo, seuif97 — MIT and/or Apache-2.0. Phase equilibria (SAFT
  family, cubic equations of state, flash) and IAPWS-IF97 water/steam.
- diffsol — MIT, Copyright (c) Martin Robinson. Stiff ODE/DAE integration for
  reaction kinetics.
- NASA CEA thermodynamic data — Apache-2.0 (github.com/nasa/cea). Gas and
  condensed-phase thermochemistry (NASA polynomials).
- PubChem (NCBI/NLM) and Wikidata (CC0) — species properties and hazard
  classifications, with per-record source attribution reproduced in-app.
- Harmonised hazard classifications from CLP Annex VI via EUR-Lex, reused with
  acknowledgment per EU legislation reuse policy.
- Reaction-QM (CC BY 4.0, Kang et al., Sci Data 2026) — precomputed reaction
  energetics, cited per record where used.

Curated data
- Kerotakis' own curated chemistry data (the codex: reactions, observations,
  register copy, colour and property curation) is licensed CC BY-SA 4.0,
  separately from the AGPL-3.0 code. Where it incorporates or is checked
  against third-party datasets, those are named with their own terms per
  record — and where an upstream's licence claim appears inconsistent with
  its own sources, Kerotakis honours the original source's terms.

Reactivity screening
- The reactive-group compatibility screen is Kerotakis' own implementation of
  the methodology published in open-access literature by NOAA's Office of
  Response and Restoration with the EPA and the Center for Chemical Process
  Safety. It does not contain or reproduce the CAMEO Chemicals database or any
  of its contributed proprietary fields.

Optional, per-platform
- CoolProp — MIT, Copyright (c) Ian Bell et al. Pure-component thermophysical
  properties; used only in builds/targets where its binaries are available (not
  part of the core stack).

Build-time only (not distributed with binaries)
- xtb / CREST — LGPL-3.0, Copyright (c) Grimme group. Used offline to compute
  reaction energetics and vibrational spectra that are baked into the curated
  library as data. Neither binary nor library is shipped, so no LGPL-3.0
  relinking obligation attaches to distributed builds.
